{"title":"2020 USOJMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9c962c48a8212d820fe7de76de8be732bfea98b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,b_1),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/21838fee38b5b2e4733ba6878a65eedc3a3f4cf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_2,b_2),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d590e27cc4eb8c6ff80a813f227d96bd4d9770f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"5\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a83ddcdda3f888e11d8b786ea13f4e093930d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{100},b_{100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> are distinct ordered pairs of nonnegative integers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> denote the number of pairs of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887919dfbc86eebc29e0373f98f97dbf23a0ae23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i,j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a835cf2c319d9462a32bfe265e830aa31c6f1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f65e6c55bf9ae77ca03bccbc6ea1d48c8b35ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_ib_j-a_jb_i|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. Determine the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> over all possible choices of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pairs.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811480f547c16afc74ffca555e4fd6c166ccfa68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> good if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455754e8d3073cfeae0813cf8e0e3766d048ee5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i &lt; j \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f65e6c55bf9ae77ca03bccbc6ea1d48c8b35ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_ib_j-a_jb_i|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. Note that we can reorder the pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f308902930acfcbfbdaa3f6e736d05d701f72122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1, b_1), (a_2, b_2), \\ldots, (a_{100}, b_{100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" /> without changing the number of good pairs. Thus, we can reorder them so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0fdabfe2f061b80c8bea92b2108c359b6ab05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1\\leq a_2\\leq\\ldots\\leq a_{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"14\" />. Furthermore, reorder them so that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5bb8d8c20eb159c1b6e650aae128937575e0fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8b76bca5358138116d4d962e20e582bfa708b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc1c96666ca3faf6045028fa37915b94e8b2f47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i&lt;b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Now I claim the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175ca598d8b65464af7c080bc4f871b648c1e358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{197}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. First, we will show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e125ddbc03e40cf2c5814e530e84d432feb31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\leq 197$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The key claim is that for any fixed integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2fb50c503f47c0baeffbfe26aa841454f65a68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq m \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />, then there are at most 2 values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf563e37d97234567a5b4d1c9e35160c4c5565c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> with the pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301d1e85ba28e46025a82d6949a6ee8c9ad64bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> good. We will prove this with contradiction.\n</p><p>Assume there are 3 integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301d1e85ba28e46025a82d6949a6ee8c9ad64bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a9a5e23d45e9aad09b6e3f14c7b5d1f09827dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(j, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c59026ee0f0757511543acb0df466247d1e8443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> are all good. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b043bedc70c6a1a546a21f75948fd15c8d4e6de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(a_m, b_m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22474554026a4eaf51a04c23acbc24bf34dc04b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_m-a_mb_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a51f281da720b82317692086c68d5aeb02433fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(a_m, b_m)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22474554026a4eaf51a04c23acbc24bf34dc04b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_m-a_mb_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95ad18c7e79c7692f627b0b1e5b30235b5552e4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_ib_m\\equiv \\pm 1 \\mod a_m\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"15\" />\nSimilarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/8902e0c934debf2502b7ef4446d11ad47d8aeae7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_jb_m\\equiv \\pm 1 \\mod a_m\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/3064a7b7027800091e5c05c415da11c92435ca6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_kb_m\\equiv \\pm 1 \\mod a_m\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a51f281da720b82317692086c68d5aeb02433fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(a_m, b_m)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/28667c9e7bbf65ba23306e6cb19a52db72d40ec7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i\\equiv \\pm a_j \\equiv \\pm a_k \\mod a_m\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, from our reordering we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed695804c900ef91198c7df56c9a380e49a334a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq a_i&lt;a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d5f7da1bdf429e231a56af6ca0742f955f6349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq a_j&lt;a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6dcdeaad4df5679ff7288c36c6d79e3a015b929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq a_k&lt;a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />. Thus our congruence gives us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc0c338bd702a079e8148d39dd07e801f88c7c41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j=a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a51d7ddaed43b3c287f6480e5513ff5b38cdaeeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j=a_m-a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />, and similar for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />. Thus at least two of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e96ba1d22002994a4c7626ba500f75dce0f7f536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i, a_j, a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> are equal. WLOG let them be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />. Now we have 4 cases.\n</p><p><b>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72b3fee730cc757aaadca3ae8383960e0840987a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /></b>\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22474554026a4eaf51a04c23acbc24bf34dc04b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_m-a_mb_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d59d8bfc82441812eb9be55a612113695f43eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_jb_m-a_mb_j=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"17\" />, so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5bb8d8c20eb159c1b6e650aae128937575e0fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> we can subtract the two equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3b1f0e94ade7c773ca29d99f5435e2af24b93b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_mb_i-a_mb_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/36430d85756de08cfdd89c6bce9d21f5d0208b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm 2, 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72b3fee730cc757aaadca3ae8383960e0840987a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706adaf2e016a3bcd4ce1a85bb40c0e3c3b1b5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_m(b_i-b_j)|\\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" /> implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b6c0341576a4881d0d4f80e16aa61e72b7884e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. But all pairs are distinct and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5bb8d8c20eb159c1b6e650aae128937575e0fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />, so this is a contradiction. \n</p><p><b>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0a79928d2b48647e8c16777503476a372d9494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /></b>\n</p><p>We have 2 subcases.\n</p><p><b>Subcase 2a: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da514e5dfa4c39951dfb2ada47ffc5aae6564979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i\\equiv a_j\\equiv a_k\\equiv 1 \\mod a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"17\" /></b>\n</p><p>Clearly we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f3bbaee807b9a1a469c983d50759427614c3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_j=a_k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" /> in this case, as all 3 variables are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0a79928d2b48647e8c16777503476a372d9494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/5083e7496b37c0240d519f6469fa85c5f951f373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot b_m-a_mb_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf105f9e306331d503d462d6bc42867cd7e07fdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot b_m-a_mb_j=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce28557022e4d46004fc912143b2d50758ec8b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot b_m-a_mb_k=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" />. So at least 2 of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbbf3e10280b5771976f3342b10181e4b31d4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> must be equal, but this contradicts the fact that all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4acea637314ebd710a727a16b98620b5b65f670b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_x, b_x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> are distinct.\n</p><p><b>Subcase 2b: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f4c00af768b1dc406132d4aa9f2aa712280a41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i\\equiv a_j\\equiv a_k\\equiv 0 \\mod a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"17\" /></b>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> must be even in this case, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1ddf57a1507686a49e3d290b3542ccac565cd35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> is also even then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c00198cf6b9f3562fd283a0733fd445489c77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_m-a_mb_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> must be even, which contradicts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea2314f36131d8da4b01ea82bd84590623a4f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_ib_m-a_mb_i|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7caed0484fd0f034fad4222c4efb563ee56d3920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /></b>\n</p><p>We must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a625bcce68f62485155ef4dcca3c9c3ee4194dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=0,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />, and similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />. Thus at least 2 of the 3 must be equal. Now we have 2 subcases again.\n</p><p><b>Subcase 3a: 2 of the 3 are equal to 0</b>\n</p><p>WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/97707a5dd159c8d85717d64e7d31fe147842ed2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_j=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22474554026a4eaf51a04c23acbc24bf34dc04b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_m-a_mb_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7caed0484fd0f034fad4222c4efb563ee56d3920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1390fb3cb6af6b4efdb1f49b8a34a6c21bff0f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> is nonnegative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d599dc5535d13ff701f42e739a9a4ba40a00763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fd895b3db00147db23ec025eb28887db42e1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_j=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />, but all pairs are distinct so we have a contradiction.\n</p><p><b>Subcase 3b: 2 of the 3 are equal to 1</b>\n</p><p>WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/97707a5dd159c8d85717d64e7d31fe147842ed2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_j=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22474554026a4eaf51a04c23acbc24bf34dc04b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_m-a_mb_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/50574d2bd9e4566c462481e4df5975198e0a941f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_m-b_i=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1da29bb29b98666fbf7b9ae44da8ed920f20e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c1a0aea07ae6cbe0b8d0551373e25c46075eed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, so by our ordering of the pairs we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a0c534375fd2fe27baf3a4832fdaf2a696ad72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i&lt;b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6defa54cba6ad3c5aece142ec051b2a06838a621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_m-b_i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />. But similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce9e4881b5453bc08ce19f3b8f24f1329dde62c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_m-b_j=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b6c0341576a4881d0d4f80e16aa61e72b7884e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, which is a contradiction to all pairs being distinct.\n</p><p><b>Case 4: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/53123a748d2dc0ab1459aaa9eff025637919d004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /></b>\n</p><p>We must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e21bbcc8b1a1db90a76c7cda79b37d049509a5a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84ec7422ed4652d699077b007d79d14dcc38e343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq a_i\\leq a_m=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356fb98df37554f7a039e96d1d1be00adbccbd0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_m-a_mb_i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea2314f36131d8da4b01ea82bd84590623a4f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_ib_m-a_mb_i|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, contradiction.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Thus our claim is proved. Now for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b5800f5ad040d308609190ef18a9e0ca08a9b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, there is clearly no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9f4e2153bb5619bcc36507b21218d906624d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i &lt; m \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301d1e85ba28e46025a82d6949a6ee8c9ad64bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> good. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3eaf8047a3f5bebfc5c43e27123a15a44d7540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, there is at most one value of i with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9f4e2153bb5619bcc36507b21218d906624d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i &lt; m \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301d1e85ba28e46025a82d6949a6ee8c9ad64bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> good (namely, this is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed4b89a6aeb4814026a2be01bde8bd7d264b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />). By our claim, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdeeee8525ac9b94678ae9207c8f1d7f2d332d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2&lt;m\\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" /> there are at most 2 values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9f4e2153bb5619bcc36507b21218d906624d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i &lt; m \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301d1e85ba28e46025a82d6949a6ee8c9ad64bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> good, so adding these up gives at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1a82635d081ff22f2e716c8793c242ec621501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 98+1=197$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" /> good pairs. Now we will show that 197 good pairs is achievable. \n</p><p>The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/5553ea8a9d07a029708059cf69387cb862ba4ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1), (1,2), (2,3),\\ldots ,(99,100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" /> has 197 good pairs - namely, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/0/b900282f111385984b8d9b785dc3162c70d6d4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> is good for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03ea81f3f2e8b2aa93118d3003a655c6c19f7e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;n\\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649071df9d6396b3a0374fadf97c23dee8ffbf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, i+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> is good for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46adcb240312765410941b1921ccefc5b9ec2c0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;i&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />. This adds up for a total of 197 good pairs, so we are done. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~MortemEtInteritum\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a295c9e5ddb88d843a73ef549392ae0ebd716e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-3$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/8015c170064215e1f21d9ce783c5aaae373f35af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$197$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />), where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is to be replaced with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>The problem essentially counts unordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/74007be33daea5ff2b11838db48328141ce37d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P,Q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> of lattice points so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af8bd418bbfcc17ee85fd2d959d120c3df86222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$POQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> due to Shoelace (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the origin).\n</p><p>For a construction, take the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/76447ce1680cf7b385a0ed2c9dca6913f6929b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1),(1,1),(1,2), \\dots (1,n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We now show by induction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a295c9e5ddb88d843a73ef549392ae0ebd716e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-3$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> is the maximum, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> obviously holds as a base case.\n</p><p>To reduce to the inductive hypothesis of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> points from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points, we are allowed to consider the point with the greatest sum of coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The key claim is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is part of at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs (triangles) with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Before we proceed, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> must have relatively prime coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, or else any triangles found can be reduced down by a greatest common factor along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/996c4f896a36f88a3fffd8d25755fd27552dffd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, impossible since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is the minimum positive area.\n</p><p>Call the hypothetical point(s) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. With triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/0390d10ca030081f94d1bd001d15910381055e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XOR$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, we know the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/996c4f896a36f88a3fffd8d25755fd27552dffd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, so indeed the locus of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is two lines evenly spaced next to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/996c4f896a36f88a3fffd8d25755fd27552dffd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> each parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/996c4f896a36f88a3fffd8d25755fd27552dffd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> (before we consider the lattice condition).\n</p><p>When we add in the lattice condition, we see that each of these two lines contain at most one valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. This is because if two lattice points with non-negative integers lied on one of these lines, one would have to be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> more than the other on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinates and a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> more on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinates. This contradicts the coordinate sum maximality of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, by deleting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we lose at most two pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea46c1ae1043a227750c91b01a7febf29f8765d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(X,R)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, completing the induction and the problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO\">2020 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013232\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.064 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.087 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 856/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28822/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.625      1 -total\n 68.65%   12.099      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 29.49%    5.198      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18976:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013232 and revision id 199255. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}